<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karpathos</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karpathos is a mountainous Greek island in the south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean Sea</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, now part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dodecanese">Dodecanese</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellenistic-period">Hellenistic period</a> it was ruled by Rhodes, and it later passed through Byzantine, Venetian, Ottoman and Italian rule before joining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karpathos.jpg" alt="Karpathos" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Magnus.chronicles · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karpathos_Menetes_Pigadia_MO3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
